FenrirOS has no systemd: PVE::Systemd's D-Bus calls are replaced.
- enter_systemd_scope() creates the cgroup v2 directory <Slice>/<unit>.scope
  itself (where systemd would, so PVE::CGroup still finds qemu.slice/<vmid>.scope),
  enables the controllers, sets cpu.weight / cpu.max from CPUWeight, CPUShares
  and CPUQuota, and moves the calling process in. KillMode, SendSIGKILL,
  TimeoutStopUSec, After and Before are ignored (no manager owns the scope).
- wait_for_unit_removed() waits until the scope's cgroup is empty and removes it.
- is_unit_active() checks a scope's cgroup, or asks the systemctl stand-in
  (/usr/libexec/pve-fenrir/systemctl, files/fenrir-systemctl) about a dinit service.
- systemd_call() dies (no D-Bus API); Net::DBus is no longer loaded here.
- get_timezone/set_timezone/list_timezones use /etc/localtime, /etc/timezone and
  tzdata.zi instead of timedatectl.
notify() is kept (it is a no-op without NOTIFY_SOCKET).
Written for FenrirOS.

